import json
import numpy as np


def aggregate(payload):
    result=[]
    for k in sorted({r['regions'] for r in payload['results']}):
        for method in sorted({r['method'] for r in payload['results']}):
            for probes in sorted({r['probes'] for r in payload['results'] if r['regions']==k}):
                rows=[r for r in payload['results'] if r['regions']==k and r['method']==method and r['probes']==probes]
                keys=[x for x,v in rows[0].items() if isinstance(v,(float,int))]
                row={x:float(np.mean([r[x] for r in rows])) for x in keys}
                row.update(method=method,regions=k,probes=probes,region_hit_sd=float(np.std([r['region_hit'] for r in rows],ddof=1)))
                result.append(row)
    return result


def report(payload,out):
    rows=aggregate(payload)
    lines=['# BGE-small / WikiQA region-routing results','','Three training seeds; official held-out answerable questions; global answer corpus.','',
           '| Regions | Probes | Method | Any-answer region hit | Answer coverage | Corpus searched | nDCG@10 |',
           '|---:|---:|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
    for r in rows:
        lines.append(f"| {r['regions']} | {r['probes']} | {r['method']} | {r['region_hit']:.4f} | {r['answer_region_coverage']:.4f} | {r['corpus_fraction']:.4f} | {r['ndcg@10']:.4f} |")
    (out/'summary.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
    compact={'rows':rows,'provenance':payload['provenance'],'dense':payload['dense_baseline'],'partitions':payload['partitions']}
    (out/'explorer.html').write_text(HTML.replace('__DATA__',json.dumps(compact).replace('</','<\\/')))


HTML='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Probabilistic Retrieval Fields — Region routing</title>
<style>:root{color-scheme:light;font:16px system-ui;background:#f4f4ef;color:#193238}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{max-width:1120px;margin:auto;padding:48px 28px}small{color:#526c72;letter-spacing:.13em}h1{font-size:clamp(32px,5vw,58px);letter-spacing:-.05em;line-height:1.05;max-width:850px}h2{font-size:25px}p{line-height:1.65;max-width:850px}.lead{font-size:20px;color:#3c555b}.flow{display:flex;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:32px 0}.flow span{padding:12px 16px;background:#e1e9e6}.controls{display:flex;gap:24px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:28px 0}select{font:inherit;padding:9px;margin-left:8px;background:#fff;color:#193238;border:1px solid #b8c6c4;border-radius:4px}canvas{width:100%;height:360px}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}td,th{padding:12px 9px;text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid #ccd6d2}th{font-size:13px}.scroll{overflow:auto}.stats{display:flex;gap:45px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:35px 0}.stats strong{display:block;font-size:28px;letter-spacing:-.03em}.stats span{color:#526c72}section{margin-top:48px}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;font:13px monospace}a{color:#17646b}.note{border-left:3px solid #d38742;padding-left:18px}@media(max-width:600px){body{padding:28px 16px}.stats{gap:20px}td,th{padding:9px 6px}}</style>
<body><small>PROBABILISTIC RETRIEVAL FIELDS / RESEARCH EXPLORER</small>
<h1>Find the neighborhood.<br>Then find the answer.</h1>
<p class="lead">Can a small router learn where relevant answers live—without changing the embedding model?</p>
<div class="flow"><span>Question</span><span>→ Frozen BGE-small</span><span>→ Region probabilities</span><span>→ Search selected regions</span></div>
<p>Fine-tuning an embedding model can improve domain alignment, but changes to document representations can also require encoding and indexing the corpus again. This experiment learns a small query-to-region model over an unchanged answer index. High routing accuracy only matters if it searches substantially less of the corpus.</p>
<p class="note" id="finding"></p><div class="stats"><div><strong id="corpus"></strong><span>unique answer sentences</span></div><div><strong id="questions"></strong><span>held-out answerable questions</span></div><div><strong>384</strong><span>frozen embedding dimensions</span></div><div><strong>3</strong><span>training seeds</span></div></div>
<div class="controls"><label>Partition granularity<select id="regions"></select></label><label>Regions searched<select id="probes"></select></label><label>Vertical axis<select id="metric"><option value="region_hit">Any-answer region hit</option><option value="answer_region_coverage">Relevant-answer coverage</option><option value="ndcg@10">Final nDCG@10</option></select></label></div>
<canvas id="chart" aria-label="Routing quality versus fraction of corpus searched"></canvas>
<p id="selection" aria-live="polite"></p><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Region hit ± seed SD</th><th>Answer coverage</th><th>Corpus searched</th><th>nDCG@10</th><th>Mean latency</th></tr></thead><tbody id="table"></tbody></table></div>
<p class="note">Searching every region gives perfect region coverage by construction. It is the no-pruning endpoint, not a routing success. Learned probabilities use supervision; nearest-centroid routing uses only frozen geometry.</p>
<section><h2>What the probabilities mean</h2><p>The training target is the region containing a uniformly drawn labeled relevant answer. Several answer regions can receive probability mass for the same question. The router is a 64-unit residual MLP on top of centroid similarities. Top-probability routing and stochastic sampling use the same trained model; sampling uses distinct regions without replacement.</p><p>The corpus is partitioned using document-only spherical k-means. Inside selected regions, answers are ranked by cosine similarity with the unchanged question embedding. A router can recover a missed neighborhood, but it cannot repair the order of answers within that neighborhood.</p></section>
<section><h2>A benchmark, with a clearly defined adaptation</h2><p><a href="https://huggingface.co/datasets/microsoft/wiki_qa">WikiQA</a> provides questions, candidate answer sentences, and relevance labels. We preserve its official question splits and exclude questions with no labeled positive from this answer-location task. All unique answer sentences form one searchable corpus. This is an adapted global retrieval task, not the official candidate-restricted WikiQA leaderboard. Unjudged cross-question answers may be relevant.</p><p><a href="https://huggingface.co/BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5">BGE-small-en-v1.5</a> is frozen. Its recommended retrieval instruction is added to questions only. The router is trained from relevance labels; no test labels are used to fit partitions, train the router, or select checkpoints. No universal transfer or advantage over full encoder fine-tuning is established.</p></section>
<section><h2>Reproduce and inspect</h2><p><a href="https://github.com/ddrisco11/probabilistic-retrieval-fields">Source, experiments, and full results on GitHub</a>. Per-query measurements, paired confidence intervals, configurations, and model/dataset revisions accompany the experiment. Reported latencies are local CPU measurements excluding text encoding.</p><details><summary>Exact data and model provenance</summary><pre id="provenance"></pre></details></section>
<script>
const data=__DATA__, $=id=>document.getElementById(id);const methods=['centroid','largest-region','random','learned-top','learned-sample'],colors=['#596a73','#9b825d','#9696a1','#087f86','#cb7133'];const names={'centroid':'Nearest centroid','largest-region':'Largest regions','random':'Random regions','learned-top':'Learned · top probability','learned-sample':'Learned · sampled'};
[...new Set(data.rows.map(r=>r.regions))].forEach(k=>$('regions').add(new Option(k+' regions',k)));$('regions').value='32';$('corpus').textContent=data.provenance.corpus_sentences.toLocaleString();$('questions').textContent=data.provenance.split_answerable_queries.test;$('provenance').textContent=JSON.stringify(data.provenance,null,2);
function options(){let prev=$('probes').value;$('probes').replaceChildren();[...new Set(data.rows.filter(r=>r.regions===+$('regions').value).map(r=>r.probes))].forEach(n=>$('probes').add(new Option(n,n)));if([...$('probes').options].some(o=>o.value===prev))$('probes').value=prev;else $('probes').value='4';draw()}
function draw(){let k=+$('regions').value,n=+$('probes').value,metric=$('metric').value,rows=methods.map(m=>data.rows.find(r=>r.regions===k&&r.probes===n&&r.method===m));$('table').replaceChildren(...rows.map((r,i)=>{let tr=document.createElement('tr');[names[r.method],(100*r.region_hit).toFixed(1)+'% ± '+(100*r.region_hit_sd).toFixed(1),(100*r.answer_region_coverage).toFixed(1)+'%',(100*r.corpus_fraction).toFixed(1)+'%',r['ndcg@10'].toFixed(3),r.total_ms.toFixed(2)+' ms'].forEach((v,j)=>{let td=document.createElement('td');td.textContent=v;if(j===0)td.style.color=colors[i];tr.append(td)});return tr}));let c=$('chart'),dpr=devicePixelRatio||1,w=c.clientWidth;c.width=w*dpr;c.height=360*dpr;let x=c.getContext('2d');x.scale(dpr,dpr);x.font='12px system-ui';x.strokeStyle='#aebfbd';x.fillStyle='#193238';for(let i=0;i<=4;i++){let y=310-i/4*280;x.beginPath();x.moveTo(45,y);x.lineTo(w-20,y);x.stroke();x.fillText(i*25+'%',4,y+4);x.fillText(i*25+'%',45+i/4*(w-80),332)}x.fillText('Fraction of answer corpus searched',Math.max(45,w/2-90),354);x.fillText($('metric').selectedOptions[0].text,45,17);methods.forEach((m,j)=>{let series=data.rows.filter(r=>r.regions===k&&r.method===m).sort((a,b)=>a.probes-b.probes);x.strokeStyle=colors[j];x.lineWidth=2;x.beginPath();series.forEach((r,i)=>{let px=45+r.corpus_fraction*(w-80),py=310-r[metric]*280;i?x.lineTo(px,py):x.moveTo(px,py)});x.stroke();let r=rows[j];x.fillStyle=colors[j];x.beginPath();x.arc(45+r.corpus_fraction*(w-80),310-r[metric]*280,6,0,7);x.fill()});let learned=rows[3];$('finding').textContent=`At this setting, learned routing reaches an answer region for ${(100*learned.region_hit).toFixed(1)}% of questions while searching ${(100*learned.corpus_fraction).toFixed(1)}% of the corpus. Nearest-centroid routing reaches ${(100*rows[0].region_hit).toFixed(1)}% while searching ${(100*rows[0].corpus_fraction).toFixed(1)}%. High coverage alone does not establish an advantage from learning.`;$('selection').textContent=`${k} regions · ${n} probes: learned top-probability routing reaches a labeled answer region for ${(100*learned.region_hit).toFixed(1)}% of questions while examining ${(100*learned.corpus_fraction).toFixed(1)}% of the corpus on average. Lines show the probe-budget sweep; dots show the current selection.`}
$('regions').onchange=options;$('probes').onchange=draw;$('metric').onchange=draw;window.onresize=draw;options();</script></body></html>'''
